From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: order direct-switch probe rollback

The direct-switch setup runs after the PPE ports, flowtable and virtual
ports have been initialized.  Its failure unwind used to tear down the
virtual ports before unbinding and draining the flowtable, unlike the
normal remove path.  A rule teardown racing this short probe-failure
window could therefore call ppe_vp_put() after the virtual-port state had
been dismantled.

Quiesce virtual-port injection, unregister the PPE ports, then drain the
flowtable before tearing down the virtual ports.  This gives both normal
remove and the probe-error path the same lifetime ordering.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/tree/87bb9b326dfe7ddafb2cc8bc588e74d552a2a9b5
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
@@ -265,11 +265,15 @@ static int qcom_ppe_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ppe_debugfs_setup(ppe_dev);
 	ret = ppe_ds_setup(ppe_dev);
 	if (ret) {
-		ppe_debugfs_teardown(ppe_dev);
-		ppe_vp_teardown(ppe_dev);
+		/* The PPE ports are already live here. Match remove ordering so
+		 * flow destruction cannot outlive its virtual port.
+		 */
+		ppe_vp_inject_disable(ppe_dev);
+		ppe_port_mac_deinit(ppe_dev);
 		ppe_flowtable_destroy(ppe_dev);
+		ppe_vp_teardown(ppe_dev);
 		ppe_bridge_destroy(ppe_dev);
-		ppe_port_mac_deinit(ppe_dev);
+		ppe_debugfs_teardown(ppe_dev);
 		edma_destroy(ppe_dev);
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "PPE direct-switch setup failed\n");
 	}
